    <bpmn:process id="W_W4715" name="W4715. Assignment Statutory Benefits, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG &amp; Home-Country Continuity" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Assignment start; statutory cycle; home-country continuity
Frequency: Per cycle + per assignment
Volume: ~15–25 active assignees
Owner: Mobility Benefits Manager / Benefits (VS-102)
Participants: Benefits (VS-102), Payroll (VS-19.2), Legal (VS-100.3), SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG, home-country schemes
Source: workflow W4715 — Assignment Statutory Benefits, SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG &amp; Home-Country Continuity</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4715_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4715_Lane1" name="Benefits">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4715_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4715_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4715_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4715_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4715_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4715_Start3" name="Assignment start; statutory cycle; home-country continuity">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4715_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4715_Task4" name="Enroll the assignee in Philippine statutory benefits (SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Enroll the assignee in Philippine statutory benefits (SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG) where eligible (residents/9G holders); manage contributions via payroll (VS-19.2) per VS-102 statutory remittance
Responsible (R): Benefits / Mobility / Payroll
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility / CHRO
Duration: Per assignment + cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4715_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4715_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4715_Task5" name="Maintain home-country social-security continuity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Maintain home-country social-security continuity (totalization/certificate-of-coverage where a treaty exists) to avoid double contributions and coverage gaps; coordinate home-country scheme
Responsible (R): Benefits / Mobility / Tax
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility / CFO
Duration: Per assignment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4715_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4715_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4715_Task6" name="Manage statutory benefits on assignment end (W4718 — repatriation or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage statutory benefits on assignment end (W4718 — repatriation or localization); retain records (VS-88)
Responsible (R): Benefits / Mobility
Accountable (A): Head of Global Mobility
Duration: Per lifecycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4715_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4715_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4715_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4715_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-712 (ensure controlled execution — Assignment Administration, Tax/Payroll, Repatriation &amp; Analytics (PA-160.3).) | - CTL-712: PH statutory enrolled where eligible; home-country continuity managed; double-contribution avoided
Owner: Mobility Benefits Manager / Benefits (VS-102)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4715_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4715_Annotation8" targetRef="W4715_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
